# Payagent — Frontend Rules (Next.js 14 + React 18 + TypeScript + Tailwind)

**Source of truth:** `AGENTS.md` §1, §2, §3, §4, §5. This file adds frontend-specific guidance.

## Project Structure
```
apps/web/
├── src/
│   ├── app/                    # App Router pages
│   │   ├── deals/              # Deal Room, Mandate Builder, Settlement Panel
│   │   ├── layout.tsx          # Root layout
│   │   ├── page.tsx            # Landing page
│   │   └── globals.css         # Tailwind imports
│   ├── components/             # Shared UI components
│   │   ├── NegotiationRoom/    # Side-by-side term diffs, utility gauge, dual signature
│   │   ├── SettlementPanel/    # Invoice (INV2-...) + Order Authorization (AUTH-...) status cards
│   │   ├── EvidencePanel/      # File upload, SHA-256 badge, Accept/Dispute controls
│   │   └── AuditTimeline/      # Immutable WebSocket event replay
│   ├── lib/
│   │   ├── api.ts              # Typed API client (fetch wrapper)
│   │   └── utils.ts            # Helpers
│   └── types/
│       └── contracts.ts        # Canonical TypeScript mirror of Java DTOs/Enums (Member D)
├── public/                     # Static assets
├── package.json                # Next 14.2.18, React 18, TS 5, Tailwind 3.4.1, ESLint 8
├── package-lock.json           # Committed lockfile
├── tsconfig.json               # Strict mode
├── next.config.js              # Standalone output for Docker
├── tailwind.config.ts
└── postcss.config.js
```

## Canonical Contracts (Member D Owns Mirror)
- **File:** `apps/web/src/types/contracts.ts`
- **Must match 1:1** with `com.payagent.common.contracts` (Java)
- **Parity test:** `ContractTypeScriptParityTest.java` validates enum literals
- **Run before merging contract changes:** `cd services/api && ./mvnw -B test -Dtest=ContractTypeScriptParityTest`

## API Client (`lib/api.ts`)
- Typed fetch wrapper using `contracts.ts` types
- Base URL: `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL` (default `http://localhost:8080`)
- Mock mode: `NEXT_PUBLIC_USE_MOCKS=true` → serves `shared/fixtures/` via local JSON
- Idempotency: Auto-generate `Idempotency-Key` for mutating calls
- Error handling: Typed error responses, no `any`

## Mock Mode (Default for Development)
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_USE_MOCKS=true` (set in `.env.example`, Docker Compose)
- Serves fixtures from `shared/fixtures/` via local JSON imports
- Enables full UI development without backend
- **Switch to real backend:** `NEXT_PUBLIC_USE_MOCKS=false` + running API

## UI Requirements (Member D Deliverables)
1. **Deal Intake & Mandate Builder** — Buyer brief → structured terms → mandate lock
2. **Negotiation Deal Room** — Split view (Buyer/Seller), red/green term diffs across rounds, utility score meter, dual agreement signature card (SHA-256 hash)
3. **Settlement Panel** — Distinct Invoice Status (SENT/PAID, INV2-... link) + Order Authorization Status (AUTHORIZED/COMPLETED/VOIDED, AUTH-... ID, 29-day hold notice)
4. **Evidence Panel** — File upload (max 10MB, MIME allowlist), SHA-256 badge, "Accept & Release Capture" button, "Open Dispute & Freeze Automation" modal
5. **Audit Timeline** — Immutable WebSocket event replay with cursor (`?afterSeq=`)

## Security Rules (Client-Side)
- **Never** compute authoritative financial status on client
- **Never** expose counterparty mandate limits in browser state
- **Never** store PayPal credentials or JWT in localStorage (use httpOnly cookies or memory)
- All financial status sourced from backend `SettlementStateDTO`
- WebSocket: JWT in connection header, not URL

## Styling & Components
- Tailwind CSS 3.4.x — utility-first, no custom CSS unless necessary
- shadcn/ui or similar accessible component primitives (if added)
- Responsive: mobile-first, works side-by-side for dual-window demo

## Commands (from `apps/web/`)
```bash
npm ci                          # Install (uses package-lock.json)
npm run dev                     # Dev server (port 3000)
npm run typecheck               # tsc --noEmit
npm run lint                    # next lint
npm run build                   # Production build (standalone output)
npm run start                   # Run production build
```

## Docker (from repo root)
```bash
docker compose up --build -d    # Web at http://localhost:3000
```

## Do Not
- Modify `contracts.ts` without coordinating with Member A (run parity test)
- Add runtime dependencies without `npm install --save` + commit lockfile
- Use `any` type — strict TypeScript
- Hard-code API URLs — use `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL`
- Disable `NEXT_PUBLIC_USE_MOCKS` until backend endpoints exist
- Commit `.next/`, `node_modules/`, or `.env*`